monitor/watcher/test-tmux-window-resolver.sh#4	bare	shell	no-sendkeys	fixture-other	Part J (your-org/nexus-code#1318): plants the NAME side of a CROSS-SESSION collision — a window in a THIRD session named after an index that exists in the first. Neither session alone shows a collision, which is the whole arrangement. No agent, no classification.
monitor/watcher/test-tmux-window-resolver.sh#5	bare	shell	no-sendkeys	fixture-other	Part J (your-org/nexus-code#1318): pads a fourth session until one of ITS indices is nobody's window NAME, so the non-widening control measures a clean key rather than the collision it exists to exclude. Bounded, and a loud setup abort if the bound is reached. No agent, no classification.
